# KitOps ModelKit manifest (docs/v2/ROADMAP.md Phase 7 "Build & supply
# chain" -- "Model weights as signed KitOps ModelKit OCI artifacts via
# Harbor; no pip / huggingface-cli on the target"). Written against
# KitOps's documented Kitfile schema (kitops.org); the `kit` CLI is not
# installed in this environment, so `kit pack` / `kit push` have not been
# run here. The point of this artifact: on the deployed target, model
# weights arrive as a signed OCI blob pulled by `kit unpack`, never via
# `pip install`/`huggingface-cli download` reaching out to the internet --
# a real air-gapped/Harbor-only target has neither of those tools able to
# reach anywhere.
manifestVersion: "1.0.0"

package:
  name: legalai-models
  version: "0.1.0"
  description: >-
    Every self-hosted model this deployment serves (docs/v2/AI_STACK.md),
    packaged as one signed, versioned OCI artifact instead of each being
    pulled ad hoc by whatever tool happens to be installed on the target.
  authors:
    - Legal Demystifier project

model:
  name: qwen3-8b
  path: ./models/qwen3-8b
  description: >-
    The self-hosted generation default (docs/v2/ROADMAP.md Phase 6 hardware
    ceiling: one 16 GB card, no 32B). Served via Ollama in this repo's
    docker-compose.yml `gpu` profile today (a `Modelfile`-based pull, not
    yet this OCI artifact) -- this Kitfile is the documented target shape
    for the on-prem/air-gapped profile, not yet the actual serving path.
  parts:
    - path: ./models/qwen3-8b/weights
      type: weights
    - path: ./models/qwen3-8b/Modelfile
      type: config

datasets:
  - name: rag-seed-corpus
    path: ./backend/app/services/rag/corpus.py
    description: The hybrid-RAG seed corpus -- source-committed, small, versioned alongside the app itself.

code:
  - path: ./backend/app/services/model_router/providers/nli_local.py
    description: The NLI faithfulness head's provider adapter (references NLI_MODEL, MoritzLaurer/DeBERTa-v3-base-mnli-fever-anli).
  - path: ./backend/app/services/model_router/providers/gliner_local.py
    description: The GLiNER zero-shot NER provider adapter (references NER_MODEL, urchade/gliner_multi-v2.1).
